# Right Wing Handball Language Gate

Hard requirement. Every Right Wing scenario must sound as if written by an experienced handball coach, not translated or generated by AI.

Use real handball language in EN, HR and DE. Croatian especially must use natural Croatian handball terminology and phrasing.

DO NOT use vague, invented or literal-translated descriptions.

## Forbidden / rewrite patterns

### Goalkeeper — never "sits"

BAD: `Vratar sjedi...` / keeper sits / Torhüter sitzt (for normal positioning)

Use concrete GK cues:

- vratar stoji bliže prvoj stativi
- vratar ostaje na prvoj stativi
- vratar je izašao prema krilu
- vratar ostaje duboko na golu
- vratar zatvara bliži kut
- vratar ostavlja više prostora na drugoj stativi
- vratar kreće ranije prema prvoj stativi

### Catch / wing geometry — never empty "wide angle"

BAD: `Primaš loptu po širokom kutu.` / wide/narrow/open/good/bad angle as empty labels

Describe actual wing geometry, e.g.:

- Primaš loptu u desnom kutu dok je krilni branič ostao korak unutra.
- Primaš loptu blizu aut-linije, ali imaš dovoljno prostora za odraz prema sredini.
- Desni vanjski vezao je krilnog braniča prema unutra i dobivaš loptu sam u kutu.
- Branič se vraća prema tebi i zatvara ti prostor za odraz.

Explain WHY the shooting angle is good or bad via: distance from sideline, wing defender position, take-off direction, GK position, space toward middle, body orientation, catch timing.

### Space — never bare "Napadni prostor"

Specify the actual space:

- utrči iza leđa krilnog braniča
- napadni prostor između krilnog i polubranitelja
- ostani široko jer je krilni branič već pomogao prema desnom vanjskom
- napravi ulazak prema drugom pivotu
- odvoji se od aut-linije prije prijema

### Goal — never vague "Vratar ostavlja kut"

Specify which part of the goal and why:

- vratar prerano zatvara prvu stativu
- vratar ostaje duboko i kasni prema drugoj stativi
- vratar izlazi prema tebi i smanjuje prostor za šut
- vratar otvara prostor iznad ramena
- vratar spušta ruke prije odraza

Do not invent GK behaviour merely to make one answer correct. Situation must contain observable cues.

## Preferred RW vocabulary (when situation-true)

krilni branič · polubranitelj · desni vanjski · pivot · prva stativa · druga stativa · bliži kut · dalji kut · odraz · odraz prema sredini · odraz iz kuta · prostor za odraz · linija šest metara · aut-linija · ulazak krila · utrčavanje iza leđa · povratna lopta · duga lopta · kontranapad · prvi val · drugi val · povratak u obranu · zatvaranje krila · preuzimanje · igrač više · igrač manje · prazan gol

Do not insert jargon only to sound technical.

## Realism test (manual FAIL even if validators PASS)

Would a Croatian handball coach say this in training or video analysis?

Would a right wing immediately know where every player is?

Can the player visualize without guessing: ball, RW, defender, GK, available space?

If NO → rewrite.

## Geometry test

Never only: good/bad/wide/narrow angle, open/closed space.

Describe what physically creates it (defender help inside, RB bind, take-off lane, aut-linija, etc.).

## Goalkeeper test

Every GK cue must be physically observable: position, movement, stance, arms, distance from goal line, near/far post relation.

If GK is irrelevant to the decision, do not add GK text to pad length.

## Tactical signal first

Every scenario needs a real signal (wing defender helps inside, half steps out, RB binds two, pivot blocks wing defender, GK moves early/stays deep, transition protects middle, RW receives while defender recovers, hips turn to ball, empty goal changes turnover risk).

Correct answer must follow from that signal.

## Register

Croatian coach **ti**: Primaš, Napadni, Ostani, Utrči, Odrazi se…

Score: Vodite / Gubite / Neriješeno.

Never mix ti/vi. No MT terms (utičnica, sjecanje, bočni branič as wing defender, Primate/Hvatate, etc.).

## Automated support

Run `npm run audit:right-wing-language-gate` when RW content changes. Hard FAIL on forbidden patterns. Manual geometry/realism review still required.
